From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/23] feat(grain): add vf_pelorus_grain_estimate_vulkan (FGS
 param estimator)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A film-grain-synthesis parameter ESTIMATOR — the dual of the denoise lever.
Grain is temporally incoherent, so a block encoder re-codes it as residual
every frame; the win is to remove it before encode (vf_pelorus_denoise) and
re-synthesize it at the decoder from a compact parameter set (AV1 AOM
film_grain OBU / H.274 FGC SEI). This filter measures those parameters on
the GPU.

A pass-through analyzer modelled on vf_pelorus_analyze_vulkan (lazy SPIR-V
init, FF_VK_REP_FLOAT, GPU reduction into a HOST_VISIBLE SSBO, submit+wait
readback, side-data emit). The estimator measures, per luma intensity band,
the high-frequency residual variance (luma minus a 3x3 box low-pass) over
locally-flat neighbourhoods (an edge gate excludes structure), plus a global
lag-1 spatial-correlation accumulator as a coarse AR seed. The per-band RMS
residual maps to the AV1 AOM piecewise scaling function y_points[value,
scaling]; the lag-1 proxy seeds ar_coeffs_y.

The filter emits BOTH the pre-reserved PEL_SEC_FILMGRAIN interop section
(codec-neutral intent + AV1 params + H.274 mode scalars + grain_model tag;
no ABI bump, the section already exists) AND a native
AV_FRAME_DATA_FILM_GRAIN_PARAMS (AV_FILM_GRAIN_PARAMS_AV1) so a downstream
FFmpeg AV1 encoder honours the estimate with no Pelorus-specific BSF. The
OBU/SEI bitstream writer and the full per-lag AR fit are documented
follow-ups (ADR-0115).

Each fixed-point accumulator add is rounded to the nearest unit, and the
lag-1 product is stored with a bias of RES_CLAMP^2 at a scale of 150000, so
the sums are unbiased and bounded through DCI 8K. With model=h274 the filter
also emits lavfi.pelorus.h274_* frame metadata: SMPTE RDD 5 model-0 values
(model 0, log2_scale_factor 2, a cutoff and a scale) derived through a table
calibrated against libavcodec/h274.c, named after the pelorus_fgs options they
feed (ADR-0161). The AV1 mapping is calibrated against FFmpeg's AV1
synthesizer (ADR-0227). Every band is measured at a chain of edge gates
(1, 2 and 4 x edge, sums and lag-1 product alike) and climbs to a wider
gate while its statistics match white grain; bands above the default
gate map to AV1 through a calibration measured through the same gates
(ADR-0229, ADR-0230). lavfi.pelorus.grain_wide_bands and
lavfi.pelorus.grain_gate_steps report the gates taken.

The shipped shader is the canonical
libavfilter/vulkan/pelorus_grain_estimate.comp.glsl, compiled to SPIR-V at
FFmpeg build time; Pelorus also compile-checks a standalone reference shader.

AVOptions: edge, strength, model (aom/h274), native, adapt.

Requires libpelorus >= 0.2.0 (pkg-config) when the filter is enabled.

ADR: docs/adr/0115-grain-estimate.md
ADR: docs/adr/0161-grain-estimate-rounding-and-h274-mapping.md
ADR: docs/adr/0227-av1-grain-calibration.md
ADR: docs/adr/0229-grain-dual-gate.md
ADR: docs/adr/0230-grain-gate-chain.md
